DailyStreak — content provenance and licence scope
==================================================

Licence scope
-------------
The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the work written for this project: the source code, the scenario
text and the drill items authored here (see "Question-bank provenance"), the English translations, the
difficulty annotations, the verification ledger, the gates and the documentation.

It does not, and cannot, cover text that came from somewhere else. The 564 AMC 10 concept-card
source entries and 600 of the 640 AP drill items are derived from a third-party study pack (below);
that markdown is committed under content/ so a clone can rebuild the decks, but the MIT grant here
is asserted over this repository's own work and not over the pack's. Neither AMC nor AP exam material
is included at all. Note also that LICENSE carries the Expo template's copyright line
("650 Industries, Inc.") unchanged — it is the licence text this project was started from, not a
statement that Expo owns the content.

